      "## Name the decision and the queue owner",
      "Before work begins on payer account handoff note, confirm which entity, period, and queue the case belongs to and who accepts the outcome. Name the trigger that brought the case into the queue. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Distinguish a new request from a correction to an earlier one. The payer account handoff note reviewer records next action, the owner, and the next action in one place. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the payer account handoff note source, reviewer, and decision date together in the payer file so a later check does not depend on memory.",
      "A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. Say which system of record governs if two sources disagree. Do not let a deadline expand a role beyond its written limit. A payer account handoff note exception keeps next action attached and routes the question to the billing manager. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the payer account handoff note source, reviewer, and decision date together in the payer file so a later check does not depend on memory.",
      "## Map the source and the evidence trail",
      "A reviewer should be able to rebuild payer account handoff note from contact list, next action, and the the payer file record without asking for a private screenshot. Compare the source and the destination values before drawing a conclusion. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. A sample payer account handoff note review checks payer file, open claims, and the surviving value in the payer file. For this payer account handoff note case, Outsourced Billing Services asks the billing specialist to write the open question and the named approver before the claim moves.",
