      "## Set the authority boundary",
      "Write the payer account handoff note authority limit into the case template, including the amount, scope, and end date of any delegation. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. Keep emergency authority narrow and followed by a review note. Write the authority limit into the case template. For payer account handoff note, compare payer file with the destination value rather than relying on a status label. The Outsourced Billing Services review ties each payer account handoff note correction to the original claim record in the payer file instead of replacing it.",
      "The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Write the authority limit into the case template. The payer account handoff note close note cites the payer file, the approver, and the time of the final check. The Outsourced Billing Services review ties each payer account handoff note correction to the original claim record in the payer file instead of replacing it.",
      "## Run the daily handoff",
      "The daily payer account handoff note pass starts with the oldest item, the unassigned handoff, and the case paused for more than two business days. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. A case that moves between owners should keep both owner periods visible. Keep the queue view readable on one screen. For payer account handoff note, the working file keeps payer file and open claims beside the decision note. Outsourced Billing Services treats a missing payer file as an open item, not as a passed check.",
      "Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Log the handoff time when a case crosses a shift. Keep the original request so a later correction does not erase the reason for the work. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Every payer account handoff note handoff names the billing manager and the field in the payer file that will confirm the change. Outsourced Billing Services treats a missing payer file as an open item, not as a passed check.",
      "## Handle exceptions without rewriting history",
